  "summary_md": "This morning’s batch ranges from radical corporate transformations to end-of-the-road dissolutions, with asset monetization running as a common thread. The most distinctive story is FWDI’s pivot into a pure-play Solana treasury platform—accumulating SOL, staking for yield, and riding a pro-crypto regulatory wave. At the other extreme, ORGN is dissolving after its bio-based technology failed to scale, opting to return residual cash through an orderly liquidation. In agriculture, ALCO blends citrus-production gains with disciplined land sales and development-entitlement progress, while LMNR is being reframed as an undervalued land-and-water real-asset play tied to AI infrastructure demand, underscored by an inside activist buying shares.\n\nElsewhere, asset-light divestitures and balance-sheet maneuvering recur: ACNT is shedding non-core assets, and RYAM faces an activist push for a full sale against a backdrop of CEO churn. Insider signals diverge sharply—significant executive selling at ASPI despite a new helium offtake contract contrasts with insider purchases at EDBL and LMNR. Distress persists in AQB’s going-concern warning and AREB’s dilutive funding, while pockets of operational momentum surface in chemicals (ASIX’s ammonia-platform pivot, LXU’s feedstock advantage) and footwear (WEYS’ margin-led turnaround, FOSL’s early wholesale gains).",
